<Document>
<name>Webb Georgia Thanksgiving Road Trip (33 Starred Stops)</name>
<description>Jordan, Janie, and Winston's Chicago to Peachtree City Thanksgiving adventure (Nov 24 to Nov 27, 2026).</description>
<Style id="star-day1"><IconStyle><color>ff329adf</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/ylw-stars.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Style id="star-day2"><IconStyle><color>ff2b5ac8</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/ylw-stars.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Style id="star-day3a"><IconStyle><color>ff8a7244</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/ylw-stars.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Style id="star-day3b"><IconStyle><color>ff40338e</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/ylw-stars.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Style id="star-day4"><IconStyle><color>ff476236</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/ylw-stars.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Style id="star-rest"><IconStyle><color>ff3a4757</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/ylw-stars.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Folder><name>Day 1: South Indy / I-65 S</name>
<Placemark><name>Start: 2550 W Logan Blvd, Chicago</name><description>Home Start: Roll out ~4:15 PM CT Tue Nov 24 after 2 to 4 PM Deljo furnace check.</description><styleUrl>#star-day1</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-87.6915,41.9284,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Staybridge Suites Greenwood (I-65 Exit 99)</name><description>Hotel (&lt;80 lbs): Verified &lt;80 lbs dog-friendly ($75 fee), $131/nt Adv / $154 Flex, full kitchen &amp; free hot breakfast.
Website: https://www.ihg.com/staybridge/hotels/us/en/greenwood/indgw/hoteldetail</description><styleUrl>#star-day1</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.0825,39.6152,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Best Western Plus Greenwood (I-65 Exit 99)</name><description>Hotel (&lt;=80 lbs): Top budget Exit 99 pick! 4.2 stars, verified &lt;=80 lbs ($25 pet fee), free breakfast (~$116 OTA / ~$144 direct all-in).
Website: https://www.bestwestern.com/en_US/book/hotel-rooms.15127.html</description><styleUrl>#star-day1</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.0811,39.6129,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>La Quinta Columbus-Edinburgh (I-65 Exit 76B)</name><description>Hotel (&lt;=75 lbs): Best overall budget corridor pick! 4.2 stars, verified &lt;=75 lbs ($25 fee), free hot breakfast (~$116 to $125 all-in, trims 25 min off Day 2!).
Website: https://www.wyndhamhotels.com/laquinta/columbus-indiana/la-quinta-columbus-edinburgh/overview</description><styleUrl>#star-day1</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-85.9481,39.2662,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Oaken Barrel Brewing Co. (Greenwood)</name><description>Easy Dinner: Cozy Indiana comfort food right near I-65 Exit 99 Greenwood.
Website: https://oakenbarrel.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day1</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.0872,39.6138,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Revery (Old Town Greenwood)</name><description>Nice Dinner: Warm modern American dining in downtown Greenwood.
Website: https://reverygreenwood.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day1</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.1088,39.6136,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 2: Historic Franklin, TN</name>
<Placemark><name>Historic Downtown Franklin Main Street</name><description>Walking &amp; Shops: Flat brick sidewalks, Better Cities for Pets green paw stickers, and water bowls outside boutiques!
Website: https://visitfranklin.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.8689,35.9251,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Frothy Monkey (Downtown Franklin)</name><description>Coffee &amp; Patio: All-day cafe inside a historic church manse with spacious dog-friendly patio.
Website: https://frothymonkey.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.8712,35.9228,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Merridee's Breadbasket</name><description>Bakery &amp; Cafe: Iconic Franklin scratch bakery for cinnamon rolls, soup, sandwiches &amp; outdoor seating.
Website: https://merridees.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.871,35.9256,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>McGavock's Coffee Bar (The Harpeth)</name><description>Coffee Patio: Streetside dog-friendly coffee &amp; pastry patio at the edge of Main Street.
Website: https://www.harpethhotel.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.8684,35.9277,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Finnley's Good Findings</name><description>Dog-Friendly Boutique: Chic Main Street clothing &amp; accessory boutique welcoming leashed dogs inside.
Website: https://www.finnleysonline.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.87,35.9242,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hester &amp; Cook (Main St Franklin)</name><description>Dog-Friendly Boutique: Beautiful paper goods, table linens, and gifts (dog-friendly!).
Website: https://www.hesterandcook.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.8692,35.925,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Anthropologie (Historic Franklin)</name><description>Dog-Friendly Boutique: Gorgeous historic Main Street storefront welcoming leashed pups.
Website: https://www.anthropologie.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.8698,35.9249,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Puckett's Grocery &amp; Restaurant</name><description>Dinner &amp; Patio: Legendary Southern comfort food, live music, and dog-friendly patio seating.
Website: https://puckettsrestaurant.com/franklin/</description><styleUrl>#star-day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.8714,35.924,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Americana Taphouse</name><description>Dinner &amp; Creek Patio: Elevated tavern classics with a spacious shaded creekside patio for Winston.
Website: https://www.americanataphouse.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.8681,35.9261,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Park at Harlinsdale Farm (K-9 Korral)</name><description>Dog Park: 5 min from Main St: huge fenced off-leash dog park for Winston zoomies!</description><styleUrl>#star-day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.8548,35.9369,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Drury Plaza Hotel Nashville Franklin</name><description>Hotel (&lt;=80 lbs): 4.7 stars! Verified 80 lb combined limit ($65+tax fee), ~$206 OTA / ~$244 member direct with FREE hot breakfast + FREE 5:30 PM Kickback dinner &amp; drinks!
Website: https://www.druryhotels.com/locations/nashville-tn/drury-plaza-hotel-nashville-franklin</description><styleUrl>#star-day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.8147,35.9467,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Candlewood Suites Nashville - Franklin</name><description>Hotel (&lt;=80 lbs): Lowest clean all-in &amp; closest to Main St (2.2 mi / 5 min)! 4.5 stars, verified 80 lb max ($75 fee), full kitchen (~$167 OTA / ~$192 direct all-in).
Website: https://www.ihg.com/candlewood/hotels/us/en/franklin/frltn/hoteldetail</description><styleUrl>#star-day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.8354,35.9182,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 3A: Chattanooga</name>
<Placemark><name>Walnut Street Pedestrian Bridge</name><description>Scenic Walk: Reopened Oct 3, 2026! Iconic flat wooden-plank pedestrian bridge high over the Tennessee River.</description><styleUrl>#star-day3a</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-85.3072,35.0596,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bluff View Art District &amp; Sculpture Garden</name><description>Scenic Walk &amp; Art: Ivy-covered cobblestone lanes, outdoor River Gallery Sculpture Garden, and Rembrandts courtyard.
Website: https://www.bluffviewartdistrictchattanooga.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day3a</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-85.3059,35.0558,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Coolidge Park (NorthShore)</name><description>Riverfront Park: Wide flat grassy riverfront park right across Walnut Street Bridge for Winston.</description><styleUrl>#star-day3a</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-85.3087,35.0616,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Frazier Avenue Shops (Almanac Supply &amp; Plum Nelly)</name><description>NorthShore Shops: Cute NorthShore indie boutique strip (window-shop Thanksgiving Day &amp; bookmark for our weekend trip back!).
Website: https://almanacsupplyco.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day3a</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-85.3081,35.0631,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Point Park Overlook (Lookout Mountain)</name><description>Zero-Walk View: Optional 10-min scenic drive up Lookout Mountain for sweeping valley views right from the car.</description><styleUrl>#star-day3a</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-85.349,35.011,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Elsie's Daughter (Chattanooga Choo Choo)</name><description>Thanksgiving Backup: Backup Thanksgiving lunch: 3-course prix fixe ($95/adult), open 2:00 &amp; 2:15 PM ET.
Website: https://www.opentable.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day3a</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-85.3075,35.0372,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 3B: Trilith Guesthouse</name>
<Placemark><name>Trilith Guesthouse &amp; Prologue Thanksgiving Feast</name><description>Thanksgiving Stay &amp; Feast: Boutique Marriott Tribute hotel (&lt;=75 lbs dog approved!). Prologue Thanksgiving Feast 11 AM to 6 PM ET ($70/adult, last seating 5 PM).
Website: https://www.opentable.com/booking/experiences-availability?rid=1340353&amp;restref=1340353&amp;experienceId=810853</description><styleUrl>#star-day3b</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-84.5023,33.4737,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Harvest &amp; Grace (Town at Trilith)</name><description>Fri Morning Coffee: Specialty lattes &amp; scratch breakfast with spacious dog-friendly patio (water stations &amp; leash tie-downs!).
Website: https://harvestgracecafe.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day3b</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-84.5037,33.4718,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Woodstone Bakery &amp; Cafe (Town at Trilith)</name><description>Fri Pastries: Fresh pastries and espresso steps from Trilith Guesthouse.</description><styleUrl>#star-day3b</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-84.5029,33.4723,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 4: Peachtree City Home</name>
<Placemark><name>Welcome Home: 306 Calgary Drive, Peachtree City</name><description>New Home!: Only 15 min from Trilith! Tall Georgia pines, fenced backyard pool, and 100+ miles of golf-cart paths.</description><styleUrl>#star-day4</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-84.5485,33.3614,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Historic Main Street Senoia (15 min south)</name><description>Local Cute Town: Adorable nearby Georgia Main Street with indie boutiques, porches, and coffee shops.
Website: https://www.enjoysenoia.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day4</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-84.5538,33.3023,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Serenbe Village (22 min NW)</name><description>Local Trails &amp; Cafes: Artsy farm-to-table village with wooded trails, weekend farmers markets, and cozy cafes.
Website: https://serenbe.com</description><styleUrl>#star-day4</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-84.7495,33.5387,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Rest Stops</name>
<Placemark><name>Fair Oaks Farms (I-65 Exit 220)</name><description>Rest Stop: Great halfway stretch on Leg 1 with wide perimeter lawns for Winston (pets stay outside buildings).
Website: https://fairoaksfarms.com</description><styleUrl>#star-rest</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-87.2836,41.0517,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Buc-ee's Smiths Grove, KY (I-65 Exit 38)</name><description>Rest Stop: Spotless restrooms, brisket &amp; snacks. Strict no-pets-inside policy: tag-team walk Winston on outer grass.
Website: https://buc-ees.com</description><styleUrl>#star-rest</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-86.2134,37.0558,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Buc-ee's Calhoun, GA (I-75 Exit 310)</name><description>Rest Stop: Halfway between Chattanooga and Trilith. Spotless restrooms &amp; snacks (walk Winston on perimeter grass).
Website: https://buc-ees.com</description><styleUrl>#star-rest</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-84.9182,34.4426,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
